      "hints": [
        "Recall the gain equation for a non-inverting operational amplifier circuit in terms of feedback resistor R and resistor $R_1 = 800\\,\\Omega$.",
        "Equate $1 + \\frac{R}{800} = 12.5$, and solve for resistance $R = (12.5 - 1) \\times 800$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "The amplifier in Fig. 8.1 is connected in non-inverting mode, so its voltage gain is given by $G = 1 + \\frac{R}{R_1} = 1 + \\frac{R}{800}$.",
        "Substitute the calculated gain: $12.5 = 1 + \\frac{R}{800} \\implies \\frac{R}{800} = 11.5$.",
        "Calculate the resistance: $R = 11.5 \\times 800 = 9200\\,\\Omega$."
      ],
